# PXQU tier map 'pxqu-flashnext-4xp100-150k-ub1024': Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (arch qwen4exp).
# Derived from pxqu-flashnext-4xp100-150k.tiers with TWO corrections.
#
# TARGET  4x Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB, -fa on, -c 150016, -b 2048 -ub 1024,
#         -ctk f16 -ctv f16, -ts 11,13,13,11, per_layer_token_embd pinned to CPU.
# EXPERTS 42.168 GiB, avg 2.9986 bpw, hist {'pxq2': 38, 'pxq3': 106}.
# LEDGER  per-card, NOT aggregate. min free 1.503 GiB (binding cards are dev1/dev2
#         at 13 layers, NOT the head card).
#           dev0  11 lay  11.927 used  3.353 free   (+PLE capture)
#           dev1  13 lay  13.777 used  1.503 free   <-- binding
#           dev2  13 lay  13.777 used  1.503 free   <-- binding
#           dev3  11 lay  13.321 used  1.959 free   (+head+logits)
#
# CORRECTION 1 -- hc_*_down / hc_*_up restored to F16 (were q8_0 in the source
#   file, left over from a draft its own report told us to revert).
#   ggml_cuda_small_gemv_f16 (ggml-cuda.cu:3310-3330, default ON) gates on
#   src0 F16 AND ne1 in [2,512]. hc_down is [10240,320], so ne1=320 PASSES and it
#   runs on the hand-written half2/fp32-accum kernel. q8_0 evicts 96 calls/token
#   and 629 MB onto mul_mat plus a separate q8_1 quantize launch, on EMULATED
#   dp4a on P100 -- a pure speed regression -- and it perturbs the gate that
#   scales the wide residual at 96 mix points across 48 layers.
#
# CORRECTION 2 -- expert budget re-solved for -ub 1024, not -ub 2048.
#   The logits buffer is n_vocab * n_ubatch * 4 (llama.cpp:3782-3784;
#   worst_case_tokens defaults to 0 at :7746) and lands ENTIRELY on the card
#   holding the output head, which -ts CANNOT move. At ub2048 that is
#   248320*2048*4 = 1.8945 GiB on one card and the config misses by 1.96 GiB.
#   Confirmed in a real load log: CUDA5 compute buffer 490.00 MiB against
#   207.62-208.99 on the other five, and 248320*512*4 = 485.0 MiB exactly.
#   Budgeting in the aggregate hides this; the whole error falls on the one card
#   with no room for it.
#
# NOT USED: an importance matrix. Owner decision -- measured a net negative on
#   our quants. Tier assignment is a depth x kind sensitivity proxy, with down
#   favoured 1.45x because this arch has NO ffn_norm and NO output_norm
#   (build_qwen4exp.cpp:8-12): the hc mixer is the only normalisation, so down's
#   error enters the wide residual with nothing downstream to rescale it.
#
# Consumed by llama-quantize --pxq-universal.
#
# FIX (wake 2): explicit f32 rules for every tensor with ne0 %% 32 != 0.
#   ssm_conv1d [4,10240] x36, ple_conv1d [4,10240] x1, ssm_a [48] x36,
#   ssm_dt.bias [48] x36.
#   Leaving these RULELESS DOES NOT LEAVE THEM ALONE: with no rule they fall
#   through to the PXQU default type, which is MXFP4 (llama-quantize.cpp:1499),
#   a block-32 codec, and GGML_ASSERT(n_per_row %% kBlockSize == 0) ABORTS the
#   run. That killed the first build at tensor 59/1224 (blk.1.ple_conv1d,
#   ne0=4) after 57 GiB had already been written.
#
